    s = s & "MIDAS_KOPRU at the bearing lines) drops the outer part too.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p><strong>Live-load stations (2026-11-03s):</strong> the girder also gets a node at every 4-7 Tablo 27 station (1_RAPOR, the" & vbLf
    s = s & "rows under the 'Yeri' / 'V (kN)' header, column K = m from the bearing), at bearing + K and mirrored at" & vbLf
    s = s & "L &#8722; bearing &#8722; K, unless a node is already within 0.5 mm. MAK_LL (4-7) reads its results at these nodes." & vbLf
    s = s & "Today only the transfer station (0.589 m) adds nodes: 20 nodes and 20 elements (402 &#8594; 422 / 603 &#8594; 623).</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""4-sections-and-the-hambly-grillage-rules"">4. Sections and the Hambly grillage rules</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>Reference: E.C. Hambly, <em>Bridge Deck Behaviour</em>, 2nd ed. 1991, chapter 4" & vbLf
    s = s & "(library: <code>03_TECHNICAL_LIBRARY\02_Bridge Decks...</code>; book page = PDF page - 12).</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h3 id=""41-longitudinal-members-composite-girders-hambly-442"">4.1 Longitudinal members = composite girders (Hambly 4.4.2)</h3>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<div class=""tw""><table>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Section</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Use</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Slab flange width</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>7</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>inner girder, span</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>sG</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>8</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>inner girder, end zone (<code>&lt;type&gt; - Y</code>)</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>sG</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>9 / 10</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>left edge girder, span / end zone</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>sG/2 + left overhang</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>11 / 12</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>right edge girder, span / end zone</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>sG/2 + right overhang</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</table></div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>The girder polygon is rebuilt from KIRIS_INPUT b2..b7 / h2..h7 (14 corners). Its area is" & vbLf
    s = s & "  computed with the shoelace formula, and the read-back compares MIDAS's area of sections 7 and 8 with it.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Concrete E (owner 2026-11-07):</strong> the staged model feeds the AASHTO girder design, so it uses AASHTO Ec" & vbLf
    s = s & "  (INPUT column C) as user concrete with the workbook unit weight. The dynamic model keeps the EN04(RC)" & vbLf
    s = s & "  database concrete (Ecm, column D). Measured on Civil NX 2026 v2.3: the time-dependent strength curve still" & vbLf
    s = s & "  applies to the user concrete (E at the transfer age below Ec), and the analyses after the stages (moving" & vbLf
    s = s & "  load, eigen) use Ec itself.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>The modular ratio of the composite section is E girder / E slab of that model: 1.2247 staged (AASHTO)," & vbLf
    s = s & "  1.1050 dynamic (Ecm) for C45 / C30.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Edge girders carry the cantilever slab</strong> (Hambly: the section represented by the member)." & vbLf
    s = s & "  No shear-lag reduction is applied, because Hambly asks for one only if the spacing exceeds L/6 or the" & vbLf
    s = s & "  cantilever exceeds L/12. Both are far below those limits here.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>""Use Hambly Eq."" (composite torsion)</strong>: this option has no JSON key. The macro therefore writes sections 7-12" & vbLf
    s = s & "  as an MCT file (<code>*SECT-PSCVALUE</code>, flag <code>bHUMBLY = YES</code>) and imports it with <code>doc/IMPORTMXT</code>. MIDAS" & vbLf
    s = s & "  recalculates the section properties from the polygon on import.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Section 6 (PSC value) is also written, but no element uses it.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h3 id=""42-slab-members-hambly-443"">4.2 Slab members (Hambly 4.4.3)</h3>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Thickness = tc (the composite slab thickness) and width = the tributary width (half way to the neighbours).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Bending I = b&#183;t&#179;/12 (MIDAS computes it from the rectangle).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Torsion C = b&#183;t&#179;/6</strong> (Hambly: half of the solid-bar value). MIDAS computes the rectangle J," & vbLf
    s = s & "  so the macro sets a section stiffness factor (db/SECF, IXX_SF) on sections 3, 5 and 13:</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>IXX_SF = (b&#183;t&#179;/6) / J of the rectangle (MIDAS Analysis Reference, Eq. 2).</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>The factors sit in boundary group <code>BG_SF</code>, activated in CS2 with the deck. This is needed: staged" & vbLf
    s = s & "  analysis silently ignores db/ESSF (or stops with an error if it is grouped) and also ignores an" & vbLf
    s = s & "  ungrouped db/SECF (measured 2026-11-05). <code>IPART</code> 1 applies to these plain sections.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h3 id=""43-support-diaphragm-hambly-443-451"">4.3 Support diaphragm (Hambly 4.4.3 / 4.5.1)</h3>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Flange width = min(half way to the first strip = a/2 + dx/2, <strong>0.3&#183;sG</strong>).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>If that is not wider than the diaphragm web, the section is a plain <strong>rectangle</strong> (web &#215; height)." & vbLf
    s = s & "  This is the current case: 0.3&#183;sG &lt; web. If it is wider, the section is a T with flange thickness tc.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>The section is <strong>uncracked</strong> (owner 2026-11-03). Hambly 4.5.1 suggests a cracked section; it is not applied.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h3 id=""44-visual-only-strip-section-14"">4.4 Visual-only strip (section 14)</h3>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>The first and last strips are drawn wider, visW = 2&#183;dx - diaphragm web (or the flange, if wider), so" & vbLf
    s = s & "the picture shows no gap at the diaphragm. db/SECF scales the drawn section back to the true dx &#215; tc strip," & vbLf
    s = s & "with r = dx / visW:</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<div class=""tw""><table>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Property</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Factor</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>A, Asy, Asz, Iyy (vertical bending), weight</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>r</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>Izz (in-plane bending)</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>r&#179;</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>Ixx (torsion)</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>(dx&#183;t&#179;/6) / J of the drawn rectangle</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</table></div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>The structure is the same as with a dx-wide strip. Only the drawing changes.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<hr />" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""5-supports"">5. Supports</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>At each bearing line and each girder:</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<pre><code>girder node (Z 0) --rigid link--&gt; node at Z = -(H + tc) --elastic link--&gt; node (link length lower), fixed 1111110" & vbLf
    s = s & "</code></pre>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<div class=""tw""><table>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Spring (elastic link, GEN)</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Fixed end (X = a)</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<th>Free end (X = Lg - a)</th>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</thead>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>SDx = axial / vertical</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>kE (4-7)</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>kE</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>SDy = transverse</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>fixed spring</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>fixed spring</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>SDz = longitudinal</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>fixed spring</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>ky = G&#183;A / h (4-7)</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</table></div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>Everything is in boundary group <code>BG_MESNET</code>.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p><strong>Temporary roll restraint (CS1 only, group <code>BG_GECICI</code>).</strong> One bearing point per girder end, with the link" & vbLf
    s = s & "rotations free, leaves a lone girder free to roll about its axis. In CS1 there is no deck yet, so MIDAS" & vbLf
    s = s & "reported ""singularity ... translation-Y"". Rotation RX of the girder node above each bearing is therefore" & vbLf
    s = s & "held in CS1, like the temporary bracing used on site. It is released in CS2, when the deck and" & vbLf
    s = s & "diaphragms tie the girders together. The post-construction analyses (moving load, eigen, time history)" & vbLf
    s = s & "do not have this restraint (owner 2026-11-03, option B).</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<hr />" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""6-static-loads-beam-line-loads-dbbmld"">6. Static loads (beam line loads, db/BMLD)</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<div class=""tw""><table>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<thead>" & vbLf
    P2_3 = s
End Function

