    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>CS3</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>DW_1 + DW_2</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>30 d</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>CS4</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>long term</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<td>10000 d</td>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tr>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</tbody>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</table></div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>The durations and the slab age are constants in the module (owner 2026-11-02; CS1 120 d = the deck-placement" & vbLf
    s = s & "time t = 120 d of AASHTO 2020 C5.9.3.4.2c, owner 2026-11-03). The girder age is computed:</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p><strong>Girder age at transfer</strong> = the day the girder concrete reaches f'ci, read from 4-7 1_RAPOR (row labelled" & vbLf
    s = s & "  ""(&#214;ngerme An&#305;nda)"": f'ci in column N, f'c in column J; 0.75 today). The curve is ACI 209R-92 steam-cured," & vbLf
    s = s & "  f(t) = t / (1 + 0.95 t) &#183; f'c, so t = 0.75 / (1 &#8722; 0.95 &#183; 0.75) = <strong>2.61 d</strong> (owner 2026-11-03: ""the day" & vbLf
    s = s & "  where it hits 0.75 fc""). 4-7 itself states no age in days.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p><strong>Creep and shrinkage</strong>: <strong>AASHTO</strong> (MIDAS TDMT code AASHTO = AASHTO 2020 5.4.2.3; owner 2026-11-03)," & vbLf
    s = s & "  f'c from 1-2, relative humidity from 4-7, V/S = Ac / u (girder: total precast surface, AASHTO 5.4.2.3.2;" & vbLf
    s = s & "  slab: both faces, tc / 2), ""exposed to drying before 5 days"" off. V/S is above 4 in., so the AASHTO" & vbLf
    s = s & "  factor ks is 1.0 for both.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Strength gain</strong> (MIDAS has no AASHTO curve): ACI 209 t / (A + B t), girder A 1 / B 0.95 (steam-cured)," & vbLf
    s = s & "  slab A 4 / B 0.85 (moist-cured). MIDAS takes E(t) from this curve.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Relaxation</strong>: Magura formula with KL = 45 (low-relaxation strand, AASHTO 2020 C5.9.3.4.2c-1).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Strands</strong>: pretensioned, low relaxation, fpi from 4-7, <strong>losses calculated by MIDAS</strong>." & vbLf
    s = s & "  The macro makes one straight tendon per girder &#215; strand row &#215; debond length. Each tendon runs the" & vbLf
    s = s & "  full girder length and is debonded from both ends to the KILIFLAMA station where those strands" & vbLf
    s = s & "  count as bonded. Transfer length = MIDAS ""Auto"" (AUTO2).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Strand height</strong>: z = KILIFLAMA row height - (H + tc), measured from the girder node at the top of the slab." & vbLf
    s = s & "  The ""from bottom"" option is OFF because it drew the strands above the deck (fixed 2026-11-03).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<hr />" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""9-load-combinations-dblcom-gen-and-lcom-conc"">9. Load combinations (db/LCOM-GEN and LCOM-CONC)</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>The combination names come from the reference model. The factors come from 1_GIRIS <strong>Tablo 14</strong>:</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><code>&#947;p</code> &#8594; Tablo 15: DC max/min, DW max/min. STR-4 max uses the row below DC." & vbLf
    s = s & "  <code>1.00 / 1.20</code> &#8594; the first number is used. <code>--</code> &#8594; the case is left out.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Dead load and prestress come from the stage results:</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Servis 1 and Servis 3</strong>: Dead Load, CS_DW_1, CS_DW_2 &#215; factor, plus Tendon Primary and Tendon / Creep /" & vbLf
    s = s & "    Shrinkage <strong>Secondary</strong> &#215; 1. This is MIDAS's own ""CS: Summation"" set of forces.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>STR-1, STR-3, STR-4, STR-5 (Min/Max)</strong>: dead &#215; &#947; plus Tendon / Creep / Shrinkage <strong>Secondary</strong> &#215; 1 only" & vbLf
    s = s & "    (AASHTO 2020 Table 3.4.1-3: PS 1.0 and CR/SH 1.0 for a non-segmental concrete superstructure)." & vbLf
    s = s & "    Tendon Primary is left out because the prestress is on the resistance side (Mn uses fps).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Creep Primary and Shrinkage Primary are never used.</strong> The Civil NX help page ""Construction Stage" & vbLf
    s = s & "    Analysis Control"" (<code>docs/midas/stages/</code>) calls them ""imaginary forces required to cause creep" & vbLf
    s = s & "    (shrinkage) strain"". They are not member forces, and MIDAS's Summation of forces (1+2+3+4+6+8)" & vbLf
    s = s & "    leaves them out. Changed in 2026-11-03h.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>The other cases follow their Tablo 14 column: FR (WA column), WS-X/Y/Z (WS), WL, TU+ (TU)," & vbLf
    s = s & "  PL/BR/CF/MOVE/LM71 (LL).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Static load cases (15): DC, DW_1, DW_2, Prestress, WS-Y, WL, MOVE, CF, TU+ and TU- carry load. FR, WS-X," & vbLf
    s = s & "  WS-Z, PL and BR are still empty placeholders.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>TU- carries load but is in no combination; only TU+ is combined (owner 2026-11-03, to keep the number of" & vbLf
    s = s & "  combinations down).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Removed 2026-11-03k (owner): load cases WA-1, EH, EV, ES, LS, S, IC (water, earth, surcharge, snow" & vbLf
    s = s & "  and ice do not act on this superstructure), and combinations ICE-1, SNOW-1 and DEAD.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Removed 2026-11-03l/m (owner):</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Servis 4: AASHTO Service IV is for tension in prestressed concrete substructure, not this superstructure.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>Servis 2: AASHTO Service II is for steel (yielding, slip-critical connections). It also took live load" & vbLf
    s = s & "    &#215; 1.3 into the service envelope.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>STR-2: the same as STR-1 with live load &#215; 1.35 instead of 1.75, under the same LM71 loading, so STR-1" & vbLf
    s = s & "    always governs.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>ENV_SER (Servis 1, 3) and ENV_STR (STR-1, 3, 4, 5 Min/Max) are envelopes.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<hr />" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""10-what-a-build-does-in-civil-nx"">10. What a build does in Civil NX</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ol>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Clean pass</strong>: DELETE every table the macro writes, in reverse order (combinations first," & vbLf
    s = s & "   materials last). Then GET each one: it must be empty. Leftovers get a second and third pass, deleted by key." & vbLf
    P2_4 = s
End Function

Private Function P2_5() As String
    Dim s As String
    s = s & "   If anything is still there, the macro <strong>stops and writes nothing</strong>." & vbLf
    s = s & "   Reason: a PUT into a filled model <em>adds</em> beam loads (they would double).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>MCT import</strong> of the composite sections 7-12. Then a check that 6 composite sections exist." & vbLf
    s = s & "   In the dynamic model the girder J measurement runs here (section 1a), followed by a second MCT import.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>PUT</strong> of all JSON tables in build order (materials &#8594; sections &#8594; nodes/elements &#8594; supports &#8594;" & vbLf
    s = s & "   loads &#8594; moving loads &#8594; stages/tendons &#8594; combinations).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Read-back</strong>: node and element counts, and the area of sections 7 and 8 compared with the polygon.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>doc/SAVE</strong> of the open file (not in a test build).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ol>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p>Only tables the macro writes are cleaned. Anything you added by hand in other tables stays.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<hr />" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""11-not-built-and-not-verified"">11. Not built and not verified</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Not built</strong> (no API endpoint): PSC design parameters, DynaGen, load contribution for nonlinear case, perform-analysis entries.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Not verified</strong>:</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>the stage-result names used in the combinations (""Dead Load"", ""Tendon Secondary"", ...): no analysis has been run;</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>the losses compared with 4-7 (the 03q model with CEB-FIP: 321 MPa vs 284.85; 03r with AASHTO not run yet);</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>how MIDAS's AASHTO creep model uses STR (28-day f'c or f'ci) and AGE (the API page does not say);</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>the composite-girder J is not readable through the API, but MIDAS writes it to the solver deck" & vbLf
    s = s & "    (<code>&lt;model&gt;_Eigenvalue.mec</code>, cards PBAR / PBARC, factors on BARSF); section 7 staged J = 0.02665 was measured;</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li>spans 2-6 (1-2 holds span 1 only).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""11a-limits-of-the-model-and-its-results-hambly-review-2026-11-05"">11a. Limits of the model and its results (Hambly review 2026-11-05)</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Slab stresses and shear</strong>: a grillage does not represent slab membrane action, so do not use slab" & vbLf
    s = s & "  stresses or slab shear from this model directly (Hambly 4.10, 7.6). Girder soffit results are fine.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Torsion for design</strong>: output torque must be split between beam and slab by stiffness, about 86 % beam" & vbLf
    s = s & "  and 14 % slab for inner girders (Hambly 4.7).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Local slab moments</strong> need a separate local analysis (Hambly 4.6).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Supports</strong>: the springs are fixed below the bearings, so pier cap and pier flexibility are left out" & vbLf
    s = s & "  (Hambly 14.2). This is a known simplification of a superstructure-only model and can raise frequencies.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Kerbs and parapets</strong> are load only; their stiffness is not relied on (Hambly 8.4).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Support diaphragm</strong>: plain rectangle, uncracked (owner 2026-11-05: keep; Hambly's 0.3 s flange is" & vbLf
    s = s & "  probably per side of the web, which would give a T about 1.27 m wide).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Slab strip depth</strong>: uniform tc, as in Hambly's 4.5.1 example, although the girder top flanges leave only" & vbLf
    s = s & "  2.5 cm of thin slab between them (Hambly 4.4.1, Fig. 4.5d).</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<li><strong>Skew</strong>: the model is always built square. If <code>G_VEREVLIK</code> is not 0 the build summary shows a warning.</li>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</ul>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h2 id=""12-constants-in-the-module-change-in-the-code-not-in-excel"">12. Constants in the module (change in the code, not in Excel)</h2>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<p><code>WL_ECC</code> 3.5 m, <code>NOSING_Q</code> 100 kN, <code>NOSING_LEN</code> 3 m, <code>NOSING_ECC</code> 1.1 m, <code>RAIL_HALF_GAUGE</code> 0.7175 m," & vbLf
    s = s & "<code>GRAV</code> 9.806 / <code>GRAV_STYP</code> 9.807, HSLM data, stage durations and slab age, ACI 209 A/B, Magura KL 45," & vbLf
    s = s & "Dummy material density 0, DUMMY2 0.001 m.</p>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</main>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</body>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</html>" & vbLf
    P2_5 = s
End Function

Private Function P3_1() As String
    Dim s As String
    s = s & "<!DOCTYPE html>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<html lang=""en"">" & vbLf
    s = s & "<head>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<meta charset=""utf-8"">" & vbLf
    s = s & "<meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">" & vbLf
    s = s & "<title>Manuals</title>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<style>" & vbLf
    s = s & ":root{--ink:#1d2733;--muted:#5b6876;--line:#d9dfe6;--tint:#f3f5f8;--accent:#1f5f99}" & vbLf
    s = s & "*{box-sizing:border-box}" & vbLf
    s = s & "html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:16px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "body{margin:0;color:var(--ink);background:#fff;font:16px/1.55 ""Segoe UI"",Arial,sans-serif}" & vbLf
    s = s & ".wrap{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav{position:sticky;top:0;flex:0 0 270px;max-height:100vh;overflow:auto;padding:28px 18px 28px 22px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);font-size:14px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav .t{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav .b{display:block;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--muted)}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav ul ul{padding-left:12px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav a{display:block;padding:4px 6px;border-radius:4px;color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none}" & vbLf
    s = s & "nav a:hover{background:var(--tint);color:var(--accent)}" & vbLf
    s = s & "main{flex:1;min-width:0;padding:28px 40px 64px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "h1{font-size:30px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "h2{font-size:22px;margin:40px 0 12px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}" & vbLf
    s = s & "h3{font-size:17px;margin:26px 0 8px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "a{color:var(--accent)}" & vbLf
    s = s & "hr{display:none}" & vbLf
    s = s & ".tw{overflow-x:auto;margin:14px 0}" & vbLf
    s = s & "table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14.5px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "th,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:7px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}" & vbLf
    s = s & "th{background:var(--tint);font-weight:600}" & vbLf
    s = s & "code{font:13.5px Consolas,""Courier New"",monospace;background:var(--tint);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px}" & vbLf
    s = s & "pre{background:var(--tint);padding:12px 14px;border-radius:6px;overflow-x:auto}" & vbLf
    s = s & "pre code{background:none;padding:0}" & vbLf
    s = s & ".list{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 24px}" & vbLf
    s = s & ".list a{display:block;padding:14px 16px;margin:10px 0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none}" & vbLf
    s = s & ".list a:hover{background:var(--tint)}" & vbLf
    s = s & "@media (max-width:860px){.wrap{display:block}nav{position:static;max-height:none;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}main{padding:20px}}" & vbLf
    s = s & "@media print{nav{display:none}main{padding:0}h2{break-after:avoid}tr{break-inside:avoid}}" & vbLf
    s = s & "</style>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</head>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<body>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<div class=""list"">" & vbLf
    s = s & "<h1>Manuals</h1>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<a href=""midas-kopru-manual.html"">MIDAS_KOPRU - reference manual</a>" & vbLf
    s = s & "<a href=""midas-ustyapi-manual.html"">MIDAS_USTYAPI - reference manual</a>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</div>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</body>" & vbLf
    s = s & "</html>" & vbLf
    P3_1 = s
End Function
